id: pm-gh1540
title: "GH-1540: MCP binaries ignore help and version probes before transport startup"
description: "External report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1540 against published 2026.10.21: pm-mcp --help exits silently and pm-mcp-http --help starts a listener instead of exiting. Source entry guards currently start each transport directly without parsing help. Report requests help/version before stdin reads or port binding, documented configuration and supported protocol versions, and npm/Bun executable acceptance. Intake records the source/report evidence; independent packaged reproduction and implementation remain to be done."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T00:16:00.958Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T09:06:15.658Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T09:02:50.692Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T09:02:50.692Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Handle --help and -h plus --version before transport startup; Describe supported configuration and protocol versions with a client example; Prove npm and Bun executable probes return promptly without side effects; Preserve normal stdio and HTTP startup behavior
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "Both MCP binaries resolve help, version and unsupported arguments through the pure public SDK before transport startup; publish the function and types on aggregate/contracts entrypoints and document configuration and protocol revisions."
expected_result: Help/version probes return promptly without stdin or HTTP startup and normal no-argument transports retain their behavior under npm/npx and Bun/bunx.
actual_result: Pre-fix executable controls fail as intended; linked and packed consumer checks pass; implementation head8b9c33517 passes26 required hosted checks and11001 tests with100/100/100/100 coverage. Final closure-head review and admission remain required before merge.
